STATUS: Generate one reusable transparent golden glow overlay for the
currently available campaign-map marker. The same asset will appear behind
either a fortress or a boss; it must not contain either illustration.

## Reference input

- Attach the latest campaign-map screenshot showing the available level 2
  fortress with its golden halo. Use the halo's warm color and broad, soft
  falloff as the primary reference.
- Attach the approved fortress and boss markers as secondary references for
  checking the glow's scale and contrast behind both silhouettes.
- Recreate only the glow effect. Do not copy any map, marker, plaque, number,
  frame, or other screen content.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG:
  `campaign_map_marker_available_glow.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/campaign/map-markers/`.
- Canvas: exactly 512 x 512 pixels, square, RGBA.
- Use genuine transparent alpha. Do not draw a checkerboard or any opaque or
  colored canvas.
- Center the glow and let its alpha fade smoothly to zero before the canvas
  edges. Keep enough transparent margin for scaling behind a marker.
- Export one reusable overlay, not separate fortress and boss variants.

## Glow design

- Create a broad, soft radial haze in warm gold and amber, brightest behind
  the marker center and fading smoothly outward.
- Match the reference's clear golden emphasis while retaining map detail
  through the glow. Use a restrained amber outer falloff; avoid a red fringe.
- The glow must remain visible behind both the 72 dp fortress marker and the
  smaller 48 dp boss marker after Android scales it to fit.
- Keep the effect diffuse and luminous. Do not create a hard-edged circle,
  ring, selection outline, lens flare, or sharp spotlight.
- Keep the canvas transparent outside the glow. The alpha falloff, not a
  painted background, must produce the soft edge.

## Separation from markers and UI

- Generate only the glow overlay. Android draws the fortress or boss above it.
- Do not draw a fortress, skull, boss, banner, map, terrain, route, scenery,
  plaque, number, lock, checkmark, text, frame, or button.
- Do not add a pedestal, circle badge, status ring, border, outer stroke, or
  any shape that can be mistaken for a marker frame.
- This asset is only for the current available level. Completed and locked
  markers receive no glow.

## Negative prompt

opaque background, solid background, checkerboard, visible marker, fortress,
castle, boss, skull, banner, character, map, terrain, path, biome scenery,
plaque, number, text, lock, checkmark, UI, button, circular badge, hard
circle, ring, outline, border, selection frame, lens flare, rays, sparks,
explosion, fireball, red glow, neon green, abrupt alpha edge, colored fringe,
noise, watermark, signature

## Review checklist

- Confirm exactly one centered glow is present on a 512 x 512 RGBA canvas.
- Verify the canvas is genuinely transparent and the glow fades smoothly.
- Preview it behind the approved fortress at 72 dp and boss at 48 dp.
- Confirm it reads as the reference's golden halo without hiding the map,
  forming a hard ring, or requiring per-marker variants.
- Do not import the generated image into Android until it is reviewed and
  approved. Once approved, it can replace the procedural glow without changing
  marker artwork or campaign progression.
